Peter LANGSTOEGER wrote:

> As I'm no longer familiar with configuring newly purchased VMS systems,
> I need someone who is willing to help me (probably better done offline)
> configuring a VMScluster.
>
> I want to see, what the cheapest DS10 or better DS10L Cluster costs.
> So I thought of SCSI Cluster (because of Quorum) and not IDE+VOLSHAD.
> Diskspace in the range of 20-100GB. HBS/HBR may be an option later.
> DS20, MemChan, FibreChan and/or HSG may be good products but I'm afraid
> they are way out of scope (namely being cheap).
>
> Some BA350 and RZ29 are still here, but I'm afraid, they wont help here.
> Some VOLSHAD, VMS and VMScluster License are also here, so they could be
> migrated/upgraded.
>
> So the focus is VMS, cheap price and after this high (?) avaibility.
>
> Anyone ?

Just installed a 2-node DS10 SCSI-cluster last week :-)

You'll need a couple of (at least) KZPSA's, which you should be
able to find on the used-equipment market.  Change the SCSI
address on one of them (for which you'll need to change to ARC
mode, run a utility from floppy, and change back to SRM).

For the high availability, again, look on the used-equipment
market, something like a couple of (dual-redundant) HSZ40's.

Danach ist es wirklich ganz einfach !  Sogar kinderleicht.

Roy Omond
Blue Bubble Ltd.
(certainly not speaking on behalf of Compaq)







