Jay,

The Digital PC 3500 uses an NLX format motherboard.  If you read the
standard proposed by Intel, you'd think that all NLX boards are
interchangable.  Not so.  The edge connectors are often different.

So... Take the motherboard out of your system and examine it.  The
later DEC motherboards have white stickers with the DEC part number on
them.  The 3500 is a "re-badged" (British term) earlier DEC model,
either Venturis or Celebris.  RSVP with the part number and I'll see
if I have a replacement board in stock.  The DEC part number takes the
format 54-nnnnn-mm, where nnnnn is the major part number and mm
represents a production line variation with slightly different
options.  I have some brand-new boards obtained surplus from DEC and
some boards that I can pull from working systems.  Main thing is to
get the part number right.  Everything else follows... Ben

