:Perusing the VMS source listings, it appears that if you put 3 or more
:8200 (or 8250) CPUs into the same box, VMS thinks that it has a 8370. 
:If anyone puts one of these together, I would appreciate hearing about
:it...

  I know of a variety of triple and quad-processor Scorpio boxes that were
  running within the corporation some years ago.

  The VAX 8370 variant never shipped because of issues around its relative 
  system performance gain (as compared with other then-current VAX systems) 
  and due to some unresolved bugs.  (The VAX 6000 series arrived about the
  same time, and was rather more expandable and with rather more headroom.)

  Since you're just hacking around, it'll probably work, assuming you have
  compatible CPU revisions.  You'll need a hobbyst license, obviously -- as
  there is no official license nor support available for the VAX 8370 box. 

  I have no idea what sort of performance gain (if any) you might see over
  a VAX 8300 dual-CPU system.  (WAG: probably not a whole lot.)

  Personally, I'd spend the money on a VAXstation 4000 series or on a mid- 
  to upper-model MicroVAX 3100 series (or Alpha), as they will be faster.
  And in many cases, these systems will be far faster.

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
