This MicroVAX 3600 (VMS5.5-H2) has a CMD-223T/M SCSI controller, with two
disks and a Sony SDT-7000 tape drive on the bus.  The backups seem to go
well, but, when trying to restore a single file from the second saveset on
the tape, the tape drive and one of the disk drives will go into mount
verification about 10-20 minutes into the attempt.

Sometimes a work-around works where we can start a backup/list of the first
saveset, Ctrl-C out of it, then do the regular backup command to retrieve
the file from the second saveset.  Once the file appears on the disk, we
abort with a Ctrl-C.

A new tape drive and controller were tried, with the same results.

Anybody run into this before?

Thanks.







