The Intel Multia is a nice beast.  I have run the 240 Mhz Winchip, and 128 MB of  memory.
I have one running at the moment with a 400 Mhz K6-2, which is mainly limited by memory
bandwidth.  The cache can be increased to 512KB with a COAST module, but I think that that
will only cache 64MB of main memory (or so my eyes tell me when watching memory tests).

The 400 Mhz AMD kit comes from  http://conceptmfg.com/
You don't need to pay their prices for the CPU, though, just get the adaptors and get the
best price on a K6-2.  At 400 Mhz, the builtin video does NOT work.  I'm using a Matrox
Millenium II video card in the PCI slot in that unit.

I found that dirt cheap laptop hard drives (IDE) with no cache are quite slow on the Multia
compared to drives with cache.

Eirikur





