Sure.

Get a VMS system (with DECnet-Plus) and install the NIS kit (current is V4.1
ECO 7) Then @SYS$STARTUP:NIS$HOST_CONFIG and @SYS$STARTUP:NIS$DECNIS_CONFIG

Or

Get a Win32 system and install the ClearVISN DECnis Configurator V3.0

	http://www.networks.digital.com/dr/cdc/


The MMJ port is only a console (which speaks NCL) if the processor card
is new enough (a MPC-III and maybe also a MPC-II. a MPC-I has no working
console).

If you don't have a DECnet/OSI (CMIP, GAP, ...) environment, drop the NIS
and use a cheap CISCO instead...

If you want NIS spare parts make me an offer ;-)

