I can verify that VMS Backup/physical can be used to make a working copy of
an NT/Alpha disk.  The caveats are: 

 1.  the disks must be plugged into the SCSI chain - parallel port won't do 
     it for you.  (Probably it will work with IDE as well but I have not tried 
     that.)

 2.  the disks must be of exactly the same type and size for either a
     direct disk to disk copy or a backup/restore operation like 
     (to backup) disk -> storage (tape/disk) -> (restore onto) disk.

And of course if you are doing this to replicate machines you will need
something like NEWSID to change the SID entries scattered throughout the
registry.   If the TCP/IP address doesn't come from DHCP you'll need to
set that too.

