Partition Magic will allow you to configure and use a disk that is larger than
the system BIOS allows. But it does not allow you to choose which disk
device to boot from. On the older systems, the boot device normally is
always the IDE disk - if present. On some newer systems you can select
which device is the boot device: SCSI, CD, IDE, NIC, etc.

