I think there is a sound device on the motherboard of your DEC 3000.
It is connected to a 4 pin modular connector with a telephone handset
symbol.
In the powerup diagnostics and the configuration display,
it is identified as the ISDN device. It is a mono  8 bit logaritmic device
with a sampling frequency of 8000 hz. There is some software for this
device
in the VMS freeware distribution.

There has been made a Turbochannel card AV300-AA which was primarily
color Video input and output, and also contain 16 bit stereo sound input
and output.
It may be possible to get one of these devices from one of the used
equipment brokers.
There is a 'Multimedia Services' software package that could use this cards
on
OSF/1 (Unix) and VMS, but the sound part was not ported to the VMS version.

Arne Bergseth



