:I'm looking for a SCSI controller for a VAX 6000-410 (Rigel)
:system.  

  The usual approaches: XMI KFMSA to DSSI to HSD, or XMI CIXCD to CI to 
  HSJ, or the replacement of the VAX 6000 model 410 (circa 7 VUPS) system 
  with a VAX 4000 model 10x (model 100 circa 24 VUPS, 105 circa 32 VUPS), 
  or VAXstation 4000 model 9x (90 circa 32 VUPS), MicroVAX 3100 model 8x 
  or 9x (model 80 circa 12 VUPS) or any of various other faster, smaller, 
  native-SCSI VAX systems...  Or, depending on the network and I/O load,
  acquire another system with native SCSI, cluster it, and serve the disks.

  I am aware of no native SCSI adapter configuration (controller and device
  driver) for the XMI on any OpenVMS VAX system.

