'Bout all I know for sure is that the blinking green LED means the
10BaseT port is selected instead of the AUI port. It really doesn't
indicate activity.

Some DS700s have flash memory to boot from, others do not. It may be
searching for a load host (WWENG1.SYS, I think). Do you have anything
"listening" for MOP load requests? If so, can you REPLY/ENABLE and see
if it's hearing load requests?

Then again, you should be seeing messages on PORT_1 indicating what the
server is trying to do.

Dunno... May be hosed...

