In <3992b5f9$0$231@hades.is.co.za> "Tiaan van Aardt" <tva@cellpt.NOSPAM.co.za> writes:

>We have recently acquired a DEC Enterprise Storage Array from a company that
>went bankrupt. Consequently, we have *no* documentation. I'd like to know if
>somebody can give some pointers on where I can find more information on this
>beast.

Check the CPQ web site. HSZ70 is a somewhat older design, but you might be 
lucky. The same cab can also house the current HSZ80 (USCSI) and HSG80
(Fibrechannel) HSx controllers.

>This array has 2 sections, each with 24 9.1GB drives. Each section has its
>own HSZ70 controller (or what appears to be a controller) plus an HSZ cache
>module. Each HSZ controller has a single SCSI cable running from it to the
>SCSI card. According to some specs we found, the HSZ70 can work with the
>Adaptec 2944 controller (a differential controller).

That is correct. The host interface of the HSZ70 is HVD SCSI, as is the
2944. A 2944UW would be better, as it is both wide and ultra. The 2944 is
not.

>We have a "DPT Decade PM1564U"3 Ultra160 SCSI RAID Controller (which has LVD
>capability). Would the Array work with the DPT (what is the difference
>between differential and low voltage differential [LVD])?

No, LVD is not compatible with HVD.

>This system also has a console port (RJ-45) which we've made a cable for.
>The serial data pouring from this port appears to be binary. Does this mean
>we have to get some type of console application for it?

It is plain ASCII. Sounds like you use the RJ45 that is on the EMU 
(environmental control). Don't. Use the MMJ connectors on the HSZ70
themselves.

>How the this array actually work? If I understand it, the array handles all
>caching, RAIDing and other functions and presents the SCSI cards with only a
>single SCSI device (with lots of space). Am I correct in my assumption?

It can do all sorts of things. RAID0, 1, 0+1 and 5. Multiple LUNs, etc etc

You really want to get the docs.

W/

