The console connection on the HSZ70 is RJ-11, not MMJ. Also, there should be
plenty of docs on Decpaq's web site; they're still supporting the
controllers, in fact they just shipped new firmware cards a few months ago.
The console port's RS-232 and defaults to 9600/N/8/1. There's plenty of
VMS-like help available from the console shell; "HELP" is nice thing to type
to start...

The HSZ70 likes to be run at 20MHz wide HVD SCSI. QLogic and Adaptec HVD
USCSI controllers play nice with the HSZ70, and multi-host support works
well too. I have a dual-active ESA rack that services a pair of Win2000
servers over a common SCSI bus. It was strictly plug and play.

