Ever since I got my used VS3100m76, it's had trouble with the
ethernet hardware.  About 50% of the time, the ethernet test
(the last one, number 1) locks up hard during self-test.  (So
hard that the reset button doesn't work.)  The other 50% of the
time, it fails like this:

KA43-A  V1.2          ...

F...E...D...C...B...A_..9...8...7...6...5...4...3_..2_..1?..


 ?  C  0080  0000.4001
 ?  7  80A0  0000.4001
??  1  00C0  0000.0006

>>>

I've posted about this before, but nobody was able to translate
the error code 00C0  0000.0006

Looking at the board, it looks like the ethernet hardware is
made up of a NatSemi DP8392B coax interface, AMD AM7992 serial
interface adapter and an AMD 21-21672-11.  I'm guessing that 
this last chip (48-pin DIP) is either an AMD 7990 LANCE with
a different name, or a customised 7990.

These chips are all through-hole, so replacing them is quite
feasible.  Getting replacements is the problem...

The 8392 should be OK.  At least one of the big catalogue
suppliers still carries this part.  I haven't had any luck
with the 7992 yet, but at least AMD acknowledge it's 
existence.  The 21-21672-11 is probably going to be a bit
more difficult.

Is anyone throwing out any dead VS3100 or MV3100 series 
machines?  If so, any chance you could take a hacksaw to 
the motherboard and send me the corner with the ethernet
circuitry? :-)

Or, alternatively, give me a lead on a possible source
for spares.

Thanks,
Kenn



