Alexander K M Leung wrote:

> Hello,
>
>     I have a DEC Alpha 3000 workstation with an additional network card.
> After booting of the workstation, the system cannot recognise the additional
> network card. If I boot the system with CD-ROM (Digital UNIX Version 3.2d),
> the system can recognise the network card. So, how can I config the kerenl
> so that I can use the additional network card?
>
> Regards,
>
> Alexander Leung

You need to boot the generic kernel, run sizer, merge the kernel config files,
then build a new kernel and boot from that. Here are the steps:

# init 0
>>> boot -fi /genvmunix -fl s
# mount -u /
# mount /usr
# mount /var
# sizer -n NEW
# cd /tmp
# vi NEW

Merge the new controller entry for the new ethernet adapter (tu1, tu2, or
whatever) into the controller section of your existing kernel config file in
/sys/conf/HOSTNAME.

# doconfig -c HOSTNAME

Move your existing kernel from /vmunix to /vmunix.save, then move the new
kernel into place as /vmunix.

# shutdown -h now
>>> boot

You'll need to configure the new network interface by running "netsetup" and
"bindsetup".

--> Jay

