to be built into the console.  The console is a finite sized resource.  My
guess is that it isn't in for those reasons.

Unlike all other recent cards, the ZLXp-E* does not have a VGA chip or mode.
It has special-purpose logic that drives the screen in a dumb-CFB mode.  The
screen resolution is dependent on the switch settings.

The ELSA is *not* as fast as the ZLXp-E or the 3D30 (TGA2).  It is more
accurately a replacement for the 3D10 (the S3 Trio64).  It has really poor
fill rates.  There is a new server that will be in V7.3, it is TBD if/when
the server will be provided as a patch for older systems.  The new server is
faster, and supports 16-bit mode -- which will get you better performance
than 24-bits, but allow smaller pixmaps and almost as good color.

We will be phasing out the ELSA card and replacing is with the 3DLabs Oxygen
VX1 in late fall.


