To which Chris <talon16m@hotmail.com> replied:

>     Well the part you need is a DEC cable that has the DB-15 on one end and
> an RJ-11 keyboard connector and a PS-2 style mouse port. They are however
> *not* PC compatible control signals. You will need a DEC LK-20x or LK-40x
> keyboard and a DEC VSXXX-xA mouse. I have about five spare LK-20x or 40x
> keyboards laying around in my closet, I don't have a spare mouse however.
>     This information was posted from Hoff, which may prove useful. I don't
> have the pinouts for the DB-15 and KB handy but I can dig them up if you
> need them.

Is it the same cable as used on the 5000?

If so, the p/n for the cable is 17-02640-01

And from the 5000/200 manual the pinout is:

Pin    Signal     Desc.
1       GND       Ground
2       KEY.TX    Keyboard transmitted data
3       KEY.RX    Keyboard received data
4       +12v      Keyboard/tablet power
5       GND       Ground
6       MSE.RX    Mouse received data
7       MSE.TX    Mouse transmitted data
8       GND       Ground
9       GND       Ground
10      NC
11      NC
12      NC
13      +5v       Mouse power
14      -12v      Mouse power
15      GND       Ground

As for the keyboard, I had a couple of them open a while back (to clean
out the cookie crumbs) and traced them out somewhat.  Looking at the
end of the cable coming from the keyboard.

     |------------|
     | o  o  o  o |
     | B  R  G  Y |
     |___|    |___|
         |____|
                   
B - Black  - Data from keyboard
R - Red    - +12v to keyboard
G - Green  - Ground
Y - Yellow - Data to keyboard

Your mileage may vary.

I have seen a specifications document on the web for the LK201.  It tells
all with regards to keyboard scanning, translation, and data transmissions.
That was long ago, and have long since lost the web address.  There was
enough info to 'replicate' the functionality, but to start with a PC
keyboard, as John originally ask about, would be more trouble than it is
worth.  Besides, finding a LK201 or LK401 can't be that hard.  I have hauled
4 or 5 home in the last two days, all for the price of carting them off.

