"Ben Myers" <benmyers@ultranet.com> wrote in message
news:3992eae9.15430959@news.ma.ultranet.com...
> Glen or anyone else,
>
> What limits are placed by the Celebris GL6200/PC5400 BIOS on the size
> of EIDE/ATAPI disk drives?

BIOS limit for GL6200 is 7.9Gb.  For larger disk, you must use a BIOS
extender program, such as EZ-Drive, which is available from the drive
manufacturer.  These program have
some unfortuante limitation, such as not being able to access the hard disk
when booting from floppy, or possible disk corruption if booting from
floppy.  These are documented
in the fine print of BIOS extender programs.

If you don't mind wasting 1/2Gb, then you can set the drive size manually to
7.9 Gb in the BIOS and use 7.9Gb of 8.4Gb disk without the BIOS extender.
Or perhaps trade your 8.4Gb disk for someone with a smaller disk.

