Not what you asked, but:

Their normal business practice for VMS is to allow a disconnect
between what you get on disc and what you get on the machine.

So whether you "should" have gotten CD-ROM software that matches
what they installed on your machine, according to the current
President of the United States, depends on what you mean by the
word "should" :-)

For VMS, a discrepancy in this direction typically means that
what is pre-installed is much more suitable for the particular
model of machine you bought.  Since the DS20E is a relatively
new machine it seems quite likely that the new version works
much better than the old one.



