> 
> What do I have to do, to successfully use an
> additional SCSI CD-ROM drive (eg. for VMS upgrade as the internal IDE
> CD-Player can't be used for booting VMS as long as you have the INTEL SIO)
> or my ZIP-Drive (with a DB25 connector). Where is the magic ?

It is not allowed to use the external SCSI bus and the internal SCSI bus
at the same time. The best thing you can do is to buy a Toshiba CD-Rom
player and connect it to the internal narrow SCSI bus. Compaq uses the
same players, so it will work. You can add the player, or simply replace
the present IDE player.

The old DB25 style connectors are outdated. The centronics style
connectors too, but the DB25 is no longer "allowed" on SCSI busses. So
forget about your ZIP drive, or buy an internal type, or a second SCSI
controller. I think the manual of the PWS systems is online somewhere.

