Not so. There are two generations of PWS systems. The first generation
had a SCSI card. The second generation had a on-board SCSI controller.
The IDE controllers on both generations were also different, and the IDE
controller of the first generation can not be used with VMS. That is why
the AU systems of the first generation had a SCSI CD-Rom if they were
sold as VMS systems. 


