This is only partly right. It could be used with VMS by

$ SYSMAN IO CO DQA0/DR=SYS$DQDRIVER/AD=4/NOD=6/CSR=%X1F0/VECTOR=56

for the first IDE CD-ROM disk and with other values for the remaining disks.
It works with V7.1-1H2 and V7.2-1 (others not tested).

But autoconfiguration is not possible with the INTEL SIO IDE Controller
and that is why you can't boot from such a CD-ROM. But if DEQ would add
this hack to the VMS CD (maybe with V7.3 but I doubt, that they will ever
do anything for the first MIATA) then it would be possible (but this is
hard to support anyway.

