You ought to be able to mount your new disks along side your old disks
and copy from the old disk to the new disk. Then unmount the old disk
and mount the new one it its place.

The disk on which this will be a problem will be the system disk: the
disk on which the bootable Unix is found. Not being having done much
with generating Tru64 Kernels and setting up boot partitions I am not
sure a direct copy of the file system would work on the system disk. .

