D was recently upgraded from UCX V4.2 to ECO4 (while F is still at
V4.1 eco 8) and there are problems being reported on the network
with two nodes claiming the alias IP address (and broadcasting
using it).

My understanding was that you could only have one UCX alias in a 
cluster, though not all nodes had to be in it.  The documentation I
have is not specific.  The ECO 4 patch kit does list a problem with
nodes behind a cluster alias not being accessible, with the fix
going in in an earlier V4.2 eco.  Is it possible that this 'fix'
is simply not compatible when running with a node still at V4.1?

I don't do much UCX; all our normal sites run TCPware.  Any info
would be rgeatly appreciated.

