What hardware and software do you use for the X.25.
I used to work with this stuff about 4 years ago so my memory is a little
rusty.

I have experience with the Simpact ICP3232 (I believe that is what they
were called)

For X.25 there are 3 levels of communication

Level 1 is the physical.  One side is configured as DCE and the other as
DTE.
Or you need a null modem cable.  X.25 was in our case synchronous.
So you need the clock for xmit and recv.
I'm recalling from memory but I think they are on pins 17 and 19. but I'm
not positive.

If you get past level one then level two is were X.25 tries to set up a
link.
On this you need to have one size the logical DTC and the other DTE.
This determines who starts the link and how to respond.
At this stage it is helpful if you can get a protocol analyzer.  Rent one
if needed It  helps
HP made one I don't know if they still do.

If you see RR's going back and forth then the link is good.

The last level is the actual CALL to establish a connection.
Again the protocol analyzer is helpfull with this.

Hope this helps

Regards,

Cass Witkowski

