Ah yes, some of us do have good stories, but I happen to have 2.  Coincidently,
both are from the same entity.

The first, a common disaster type.  Seems the computer room ceiling had asbestos
in the tiles, and since that's now a no-no, it was slated for removal.  As
normal, not everyone was on the same page, and one morning one of the technical
people came in to find a workman standing on the disk drives, (with RP04s,
RP07s, and such, they seem a good bench to stand on), tearing down the ceiling,
and the air in the room a white haze from all the asbestos dust, while the disks
were still running.

The second is a bit better.  A sheriff's department was running a PDP-11 system,
and had VT52 terminals.  A DEC service engineer was called in to fix one of the
VT52s.  Upon looking at the terminal, with a hugh hole clear through it, he
turns to the deputy and says "I'll fix this, but only if you give me the
story".  Seems a deputy was having trouble getting the computer to do what he
wanted, and in a fit of frustration, jumps up, pulls out his weapon, and shoots
the damn thing!

