Jason,

1. The older Celebris XL 590 BIOS will not recognize a drive larger
than 2.1GB.  You can use WD's EZ-DRIVE software to work around this,
but it is potentially messy.

2. AFAIK, there is no way to boot from the SCSI drive when an IDE
drive is installed.  Only very expensive contemporary motherboards
with built-in SCSI offer this sort of setup option.

3. If your system has a BIOS version earlier than 2.04, you're better
off flashing the 2.04 BIOS to solve Y2K problems, but it won't improve
the IDE drive situation.

The 20GB drive offers great capacity at a bargain price, but you're
better off sticking with an all SCSI system.

If you need more memory for this system, let me know.  We have it in
stock.  Fast page mode, with parity... Ben Myers

