Hi,

I assume that you're running Tru64 UNIX. If so, read on...

You need to increase the maximum per process data segment size. The default value is 134217728, or roughly 130MB as you noted.

Create a stanza file and use sysconfigdb to update the proc subsystem in sysconfigtab. For example, the following will increase the value to 500MB:

proc:
    per-proc-data-size = 536870912

You must reboot the system before the changes will take effect. See the man pages for "sysconfigdb" and "stanza" for more details, and be careful not to take too much memory away from the OS.

--> Jay

