  Operating system?

  Monitors do not, in my experience, have nor need software drivers. 

  Graphics controllers do have software drivers.

  There might be some little collection of data that a particular
  operating system uses as part of its display configuration process, 
  but I'd not expect it to be anywhere near equivilent to what OpenVMS 
  calls a "device driver".

  The VRC21-HA is a standard North American multi-sync monitor.

  Most of (all of?) the members of the VRC21 series monitors will work
  with controllers at resolutions from VGA up to 1600x1200 at 75Hz.

  The following is from a VRC21-KA/K4/WA/W3/W4, and AFAIK that is a
  drop-in replacement for the -HA -- differing only in the color of
  the plastic used.  (I don't have an -HA manual handy to check and
  compare the resolutions.)

  Factory preset resolutions (values +/- 1 KHz) for the -Kx series:

        Resolution  Fh KHz  Fv KHz
    0   640 x  480  31.47h  59.94v
    1   640 x  480  37.5h   75v
    2   800 x  600  46.88h  75v
    3  1600 x 1200  81.25h  65v
    4  1024 x  768  56.48h  70.07v
    5  1024 x  768  60.02h  75.03v
    6   720 x  400  31.47h  70.08v
    7  1280 x  512  76.76h  139.3v
    8   800 x  600  37.88h  60.32v
    9  1280 x 1024  79.98h  75.03v
   10  1280 x 1024  77.13h  72.56v
   11  1600 x 1200  93.75h  75v

  There is room for another dozen user settings.

  DDC (DDC1 and DDC2B) is supported.

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
